Following was "PHYS110," a 3-credit-hour course titled Fundamentals of Physics I. It covered mechanics, kinematics, and Newton's laws, supplemented by hands-on experiments in the lab. Alex often partnered with peers for group experiments on topics such as pendulum motion or velocity calculations, finding the practical application a refreshing change from theory. The moderate credit hours suggested a balanced effort of 9-12 hours weekly, perfect for integrating with heavier courses.
