he Standard Access’s no-frills integrity. In essence, this nexus at longitude 12.492° isn’t merely stone and space; it’s a dialogue across centuries. From its inauguration 1,944 years ago to today’s tiered admission strategies, the forum remains a masterclass in balancing preservation with public access—where every ticket type, discounted or otherwise, becomes a key to time travel.

